(4640631, 664999, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>Compositionally, the shot has some merit.  The front grill of the car, which seems to be the main focal point, is in a good location for the shot to have balance.<br/> <br/>Technically, with just a bit of post processing, I think you could probably have added at least 1, if not 2, points to your shot (if that, indeed, is your goal).<br/> <br/>First, I would rotate the shot to the left, just a hair -- about 3 degrees -- not much.  Granted the "tilt" is from your perspective when taking the shot, but it still feels crooked.<br/> <br/>Then, a slight adjustment with curves or levels would probably eliminate the couple of distracting "things in the background, and they would give the car itself a bit of extra contrast and depth (commonly called "pop" on dpc).<br/> <br/>Then, I would boost saturation just a hair to make the blue tarp a bit more vibrant.<br/> <br/>It is not a lot, but it may be something that you could try to see if it gives it a bit more of a "finished" or "polished" feeling to it.<br/> <br/>Please feel free to contact me if I need to further clarify or explain myself.<br/> <br/>Karma</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat Compositionally, the shot has some merit.  The front grill of the car, which seems to be the main focal point, is in a good location for the shot to have balance. Technically, with just a bit of post processing, I think you could probably have added at least 1, if not 2, points to your shot (if that, indeed, is your goal). First, I would rotate the shot to the left, just a hair -- about 3 degrees -- not much.  Granted the "tilt" is from your perspective when taking the shot, but it still feels crooked. Then, a slight adjustment with curves or levels would probably eliminate the couple of distracting "things in the background, and they would give the car itself a bit of extra contrast and depth (commonly called "pop" on dpc). Then, I would boost saturation just a hair to make the blue tarp a bit more vibrant. It is not a lot, but it may be something that you could try to see if it gives it a bit more of a "finished" or "polished" feeling to it. Please feel free to contact me if I need to further clarify or explain myself. Karma', '2008-04-15 11:37:22.000000', NULL, 0),
